{"seconds": 619.096, "paras": [{"n": 1, "start": 0.37, "end": 13.45, "text": "The state in Grand Theft Auto Six doesn't exist. It's called", "cut": 13.78}, {"n": 2, "start": 14.11, "end": 23.65, "text": "But almost none of it was invented. Every piece of Leonida w", "cut": 24.055}, {"n": 3, "start": 24.46, "end": 38.88, "text": "By the end of this video, you'll know why the hotels in Vice", "cut": 39.36}, {"n": 4, "start": 39.84, "end": 44.47, "text": "So, why Florida? Let's start with the city at the heart of i", "cut": 45.175}, {"n": 5, "start": 45.88, "end": 52.38, "text": "In the game, Vice City feels like it has always been there. ", "cut": 52.785}, {"n": 6, "start": 53.19, "end": 64.94, "text": "In the winter of 1894, a series of hard freezes wiped out th", "cut": 65.345}, {"n": 7, "start": 65.75, "end": 85.14, "text": "A landowner there, Julia Tuttle, had been begging a railroad", "cut": 85.545}, {"n": 8, "start": 85.95, "end": 94.49, "text": "The railroad arrived in 1896. That summer, a few hundred vot", "cut": 94.895}, {"n": 9, "start": 95.3, "end": 106.68, "text": "So Vice City's real twin wasn't an old city that grew slowly", "cut": 107.385}, {"n": 10, "start": 108.09, "end": 116.65, "text": "Leonida is a state built on hustle. Get rich quick, cash out", "cut": 117.055}, {"n": 11, "start": 117.46, "end": 141.11, "text": "In the 1920s, everyone wanted a piece of Florida. Swamps wer", "cut": 141.515}, {"n": 12, "start": 141.92, "end": 149.85, "text": "Then, on the eighteenth of September, 1926, the eye of a maj", "cut": 150.255}, {"n": 13, "start": 150.66, "end": 158.53, "text": "Many people had never seen a hurricane. When the calm eye ar", "cut": 159.135}, {"n": 14, "start": 159.74, "end": 169.33, "text": "At least three hundred and seventy-two people died. Whole ne", "cut": 169.81}, {"n": 15, "start": 170.29, "end": 187.33, "text": "Boom. Bust. Reinvent. Remember that pattern, because it expl", "cut": 188.035}, {"n": 16, "start": 188.74, "end": 199.73, "text": "In Vice City, the beachfront is lined with pastel hotels. Pi", "cut": 200.135}, {"n": 17, "start": 200.54, "end": 210.56, "text": "In the 1930s, Miami Beach rebuilt with hundreds of small hot", "cut": 210.965}, {"n": 18, "start": 211.37, "end": 218.88, "text": "But by the 1970s, those hotels were run-down, and developers", "cut": 219.285}, {"n": 19, "start": 219.69, "end": 234.87, "text": "A woman named Barbara Capitman fought back. In 1979, her gro", "cut": 235.275}, {"n": 20, "start": 235.68, "end": 248.34, "text": "Then her co-founder, a designer named Leonard Horowitz, did ", "cut": 248.745}, {"n": 21, "start": 249.15, "end": 256.67, "text": "So here's the twist. The candy-coloured Miami that Vice City", "cut": 257.25}, {"n": 22, "start": 257.83, "end": 265.18, "text": "Now leave the city. In the trailers, there's a huge swamp ca", "cut": 265.585}, {"n": 23, "start": 265.99, "end": 280.85, "text": "It looks like a giant field of grass. It's actually a river.", "cut": 281.255}, {"n": 24, "start": 281.66, "end": 289.44, "text": "And it's full of alligators. Florida's wildlife agency estim", "cut": 289.845}, {"n": 25, "start": 290.25, "end": 310.85, "text": "But the swamp has a newer monster. Burmese pythons, most lik", "cut": 311.255}, {"n": 26, "start": 311.66, "end": 330.5, "text": "So why Grassrivers? In 1947, a writer named Marjory Stoneman", "cut": 330.905}, {"n": 27, "start": 331.31, "end": 334.91, "text": "River of Grass. Grassrivers. Rockstar just flipped it around", "cut": 335.49}, {"n": 28, "start": 336.07, "end": 352.43, "text": "The Grand Theft Auto Six trailers are packed with chaos. Peo", "cut": 352.835}, {"n": 29, "start": 353.24, "end": 361.879, "text": "Florida Man arrested for... well, you've seen the headlines.", "cut": 362.284}, {"n": 30, "start": 362.689, "end": 382.179, "text": "But there's a much more boring explanation. Florida has one ", "cut": 382.584}, {"n": 31, "start": 382.989, "end": 393.279, "text": "Some experts think the law isn't the whole story. But it mea", "cut": 393.809}, {"n": 32, "start": 394.339, "end": 400.909, "text": "Now, that TV show. To understand where Vice City really come", "cut": 401.314}, {"n": 33, "start": 401.719, "end": 412.789, "text": "That year, over about six months, roughly a hundred and twen", "cut": 413.194}, {"n": 34, "start": 413.599, "end": 433.079, "text": "At the same time, South Florida had become a major gateway f", "cut": 433.484}, {"n": 35, "start": 433.889, "end": 442.729, "text": "The new arrivals got much of the blame. But one criminologis", "cut": 443.134}, {"n": 36, "start": 443.539, "end": 455.539, "text": "Hollywood saw a story. In 1983, Scarface. In 1984, a TV show", "cut": 455.944}, {"n": 37, "start": 456.349, "end": 469.599, "text": "And in 2002, Rockstar took that exact mix, the pastel hotels", "cut": 470.004}, {"n": 38, "start": 470.409, "end": 484.089, "text": "So when Grand Theft Auto Six goes back to Vice City, it isn'", "cut": 484.769}, {"n": 39, "start": 485.449, "end": 508.309, "text": "But the real Miami kept growing. In 1900, about half a milli", "cut": 508.714}, {"n": 40, "start": 509.119, "end": 520.649, "text": "And all those people needed somewhere to live. So Florida ke", "cut": 521.129}, {"n": 41, "start": 521.609, "end": 522.919, "text": "And that edge is moving.", "cut": 523.599}, {"n": 42, "start": 524.279, "end": 529.019, "text": "In the game, Vice City will look like this forever. The real", "cut": 529.424}, {"n": 43, "start": 529.829, "end": 547.929, "text": "Miami sits on limestone, a rock so full of holes it works li", "cut": 548.334}, {"n": 44, "start": 548.739, "end": 560.709, "text": "Local planners expect about two feet of sea level rise by ar", "cut": 561.114}, {"n": 45, "start": 561.519, "end": 576.929, "text": "Miami Beach is fighting back. It's raising roads, and spendi", "cut": 577.609}, {"n": 46, "start": 578.289, "end": 598.869, "text": "So, why Florida? Because no other place packs this much into", "cut": 599.274}, {"n": 47, "start": 599.679, "end": 605.789, "text": "Rockstar can rebuild Vice City whenever it wants. The real o", "cut": 606.469}, {"n": 48, "start": 607.149, "end": 617.949, "text": "Next time, we're going to Arrakis, the desert planet from Du", "cut": 619.096}], "words": [["the", 0.42, 1], ["state", 0.89, 1], ["in", 1.06, 1], ["grand", 1.24, 1], ["theft", 1.59, 1], ["auto", 1.94, 1], ["six", 2.23, 1], ["doesn't", 2.46, 1], ["exist", 2.93, 1], ["it's", 3.64, 1], ["called", 4.03, 1], ["leonida", 4.58, 1], ["it", 5.46, 1], ["has", 5.56, 1], ["a", 5.87, 1], ["neon", 6.03, 1], ["city", 6.42, 1], ["a", 7.23, 1], ["swamp", 7.37, 1], ["full", 7.78, 1], ["of", 8.12, 1], ["alligators", 8.32, 1], ["a", 9.29, 1], ["chain", 9.33, 1], ["of", 9.74, 1], ["tropical", 9.95, 1], ["islands", 10.56, 1], ["and", 11.6, 1], ["some", 11.78, 1], ["of", 12.0, 1], ["the", 12.13, 1], ["strangest", 12.31, 1], ["people", 12.75, 1], ["in", 13.06, 1], ["gaming", 13.19, 1], ["but", 14.11, 2], ["almost", 14.39, 2], ["none", 14.89, 2], ["of", 15.24, 2], ["it", 15.46, 2], ["was", 15.67, 2], ["invented", 15.95, 2], ["every", 16.65, 2], ["piece", 17.07, 2], ["of", 17.5, 2], ["leonida", 17.71, 2], ["was", 18.28, 2], ["taken", 18.56, 2], ["from", 18.98, 2], ["one", 19.34, 2], ["real", 19.62, 2], ["place", 19.98, 2], ["and", 20.97, 2], ["the", 21.37, 2], ["real", 21.61, 2], ["story", 21.91, 2], ["is", 22.27, 2], ["wilder", 22.45, 2], ["than", 22.88, 2], ["the", 23.18, 2], ["game", 23.42, 2], ["by", 24.49, 3], ["the", 24.66, 3], ["end", 24.89, 3], ["of", 25.12, 3], ["this", 25.29, 3], ["video", 25.57, 3], ["you'll", 25.92, 3], ["know", 26.32, 3], ["why", 26.6, 3], ["the", 26.83, 3], ["hotels", 27.06, 3], ["in", 27.46, 3], ["vice", 27.78, 3], ["city", 28.14, 3], ["are", 28.15, 3], ["pink", 28.37, 3], ["where", 29.46, 3], ["the", 29.77, 3], ["name", 29.97, 3], ["grassrivers", 30.62, 3], ["really", 30.95, 3], ["comes", 31.31, 3], ["from", 31.61, 3], ["why", 32.86, 3], ["florida", 33.15, 3], ["